<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Livonia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Livonia is a historical region on the eastern Baltic coast, covering parts of present-day Latvia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>. It was contested by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>. Sweden took most of it in the early seventeenth century, making it a key province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> until its loss to Russia in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/livonia.jpg" alt="Livonia" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Athanasius Soter · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Livonia_in_1534_(English).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
